meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: American Community Survey
    title_snapshot: American Community Survey - Nativity of the population
    description: |-
      The American Community Survey (ACS) is an ongoing survey that provides vital information on a yearly basis about our nation and its people. Information from the survey generates data that help inform how trillions of dollars in federal funds are distributed each year.
    description_snapshot: |-
      This file contains the total population and the foreign-born population of the United States for each year from 2005, from the ACS 1-year estimates (table B05002, "Place of Birth by Nativity and Citizenship Status"), retrieved through the Census Bureau data API. The foreign-born population covers everyone living in the United States who was born in another country, whatever their legal status. There is no value for 2020: the Census Bureau did not release standard 1-year estimates for that year because of data-collection problems during the COVID-19 pandemic.
    date_published: "2025-09-11"

    # Citation
    producer: US Census Bureau
    citation_full: |-
      U.S. Census Bureau, American Community Survey 1-Year Estimates, Table B05002 (Place of Birth by Nativity and Citizenship Status).

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs
    url_download: https://api.census.gov/data/2024/acs/acs1
    date_accessed: "2026-07-22"

    # License
    license:
      name: Public domain
